INT. SURGICAL OBSERVATION GALLERY - DAY

A tiered room above an operating theater, glass wall onto green tiles and white light. Folding chairs on a stepped floor. A pot of lukewarm coffee, untouched. Beyond the glass, a quiet operation unfolds without a sound.

DR. ELEANOR WHITLOCK, 60s, chief of surgery, silver bob and half-moon glasses, sits front and center with a clipboard on her knee. DR. VIKRAM RAO, 40s, lean, in a charcoal sweater, stands with his arms folded at the glass. NURSE SINEAD DUFFY, 30s, freckled, ties off a supply bag. RESIDENT TAKUMI IKEDA, 20s, hollow-eyed, nods over a clipboard. INTERN PALOMA RIVERA, 20s, bright-eyed, takes notes with great seriousness. And Mr. LESZEK BUKOWSKI, 70s, an elderly volunteer observer in a corduroy jacket and a hospital visitor's badge, sits in the back row with a paper bag of lemon drops.

Below, the surgeons work. Nothing seems to happen. A hand moves. A suture is pulled.

WHITLOCK
Dr. Rao, how long has the cardiac been under?

RAO
Three hours and ten minutes.

WHITLOCK
Is that long?

RAO
For this one, it's average.

PALOMA
(writing)
Three hours, ten minutes, average.

TAKUMI
(muttering)
It feels longer.

SINEAD
It always does from up here.

Bukowski unwraps a lemon drop and pops it in his mouth. The wrapper crackles. Everyone turns. He holds up the bag.

BUKOWSKI
Anyone?

WHITLOCK
Mr. Bukowski, this is a sterile gallery.

BUKOWSKI
It's a lemon drop.

RAO
Let him have it, Eleanor.

WHITLOCK
I will, Vikram. Provided he does not choke.

BUKOWSKI
I'm seventy-three. I've outlived four cardiologists.

SINEAD
That's not the comfort you think it is, Mr. Bukowski.

Paloma giggles, claps a hand over her mouth. Takumi's head sinks lower. Below, the surgeon gestures; a monitor beeps; a gloved hand lifts a clamp.

PALOMA
Is that the valve?

RAO
That's the valve.

PALOMA
It's beautiful.

RAO
It's a pump with a door, Paloma.

PALOMA
A beautiful pump with a door.

WHITLOCK
Intern, you're learning.

Bukowski offers the bag to Takumi. Takumi, half asleep, takes a lemon drop without looking. Sinead catches Paloma's eye and rolls her own. Rao paces to the end of the glass, turns, comes back. Whitlock marks something on her sheet.

TAKUMI
(waking)
Did I miss something?

SINEAD
Only the valve.

TAKUMI
Damn.

WHITLOCK
Dr. Ikeda.

TAKUMI
Sorry, Chief.

RAO
He'll watch the closing.

TAKUMI
I'll watch the closing.

BUKOWSKI
What closes?

SINEAD
The chest.

BUKOWSKI
How long does that take?

SINEAD
About as long as it takes you to finish that bag.

Bukowski regards the bag, shakes it, counts, and sighs.

BUKOWSKI
Then I'd better ration.

The monitor below settles into a long, even rhythm. In the gallery, five of them turn to watch the closing, and one, Bukowski, puts the bag away.
